    id: "the-basics",
    n: "BLOCK 02 · THE BASICS",
    h2: "The Basics",
    items: [
      ["What is Critical Situation Travel Labor (CSTL)?", "Critical Situation Travel Labor is a distinct workforce category for the moments when the required speed, skill, and scale exceed what any single local market can supply. It isn’t a way to add headcount. It’s a way to protect continuity."],
      ["How does travel labor work?", "AFIMAC sources, screens, travels, houses, and supervises a team, then deploys them to your site for the length of the situation. The engagement runs in four phases: Assessment, Mobilization, Deployment, and Demobilization. You get a working crew and a single point of contact, not a stack of resumes to manage."],
      ["What situations do you handle?", "Initial line start-ups, production shortfalls, plant relocations, health emergencies, disaster response, and more. The common thread is that the cost of waiting has become higher than the cost of acting."],
      ["How is this different from a staffing agency?", "A staffing agency hands you candidates to manage. AFIMAC manages the team on site, including travel, housing, safety onboarding, and supervision. In one published engagement, a Fortune 500 agricultural equipment manufacturer brought in multiple staffing providers and retained AFIMAC as the sole non-local partner."],
      ["What kinds of roles can you staff?", "Skilled, semi-skilled, and general labor roles across manufacturing, warehousing, and logistics. Deployments have included CNC machinists, fabricators, welders, forklift operators, material handlers, packaging operators, boiler operators, and wastewater treatment technicians."],
      ["What industries do you serve?", "Most of North American industry: automotive, aerospace and defense, food and beverage, consumer goods, metals, energy, chemicals and plastics, packaging, warehousing and logistics, and more. The process is the same across sectors; the roles change."],
      ["How long do crews stay?", "As long as the gap lasts. Engagements are temporary by design and end with a planned demobilization when your permanent workforce recovers. Published engagements have run from multi-month assignments to two-year partnerships."],
      ["Can you handle a strike or work stoppage?", "Yes. Rapid, managed workforce continuity during labor disputes is a core CSTL use case."],
    ],
    spec: `<b>Elementor:</b> EK Accordion (8 items), closed state. Answers come from the approved cluster copy and the published case studies on the live pillar. <b>This page carries the FAQPage structured data for the full set below.</b>`,
  },
